RF.put("questb:b37",{"8517":{"id":8517,"t":"The Alliance Needs Linen Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 51.","obj":"Bring 20 Linen Bandages to Sentinel Silversky at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Linen Bandage","desc":"The war at Ahn'Qiraj is going to be long and bloody. It is a very wise thing that the Alliance is doing by enlisting the aid of you, and those like you, to build up the materiel necessary before plunging headlong into conflict.\nI have been asked to head up the collection of linen bandages for the war, and I am hoping that you are going to assist me in amassing as many as we need. It is no light matter, but at least the linen bandages are the least difficult to create. Are you with us, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Do you have the twenty linen bandages that I require, ‹class›?","done":"Many are the soldiers that will benefit from your contribution here today, ‹class›. I shall see to it personally that the Alliance is made aware of your efforts. Allow me a moment to store these bandages properly and update my count, and then you should check back with me to see if I am in need of more.\nMay the Light of Elune shine upon you, ‹race›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60,"y":33.3,"n":"Sentinel Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8437":{"id":8437,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"677":{"id":677,"t":"Call to Arms","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 10 Witherbark Axe Throwers, 10 Headhunters and 8 Witch Doctors, and return to Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\nWitherbark Axe Thrower slain : 0/ 10\nWitherbark Headhunter slain : 0/ 10\nWitherbark Witch Doctor slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The Witherbark trolls and Boulderfist ogres of Arathi are working together to rid us from this land, but we shall not meet our fates at their, or anyone else's, hand. We will slay them and show them that we, too, have a home here.\nThe trolls turned their backs to us; the ogres would use us for food and bedding if we allowed them to--these things shall not be.\nWe start our attack on the Witherbark trolls to the south of here. Slay them in droves, and only return when their camps run thick with blood.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"If you have not yet completed my task, then perhaps you are a coward in heart as well as a tyro in war.","done":"The signs of war are upon your garments, and sweat drips from your brow. Good, very good indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.2,"y":33.9,"n":"Drum Fel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"86757":{"id":86757,"t":"Slowing the orc advance","lv":32,"min":27,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 6 Jagged Orc Swords and 4 Curved Orc Daggers to Shandrina.\n6 Jagged Orcish Sword\n4 Curved Orcish Dagger","desc":"Orcs have taken over the eastern forest, and their scouts and grunts now lurk throughout the woods! It's not safe for our kind to move about Ashenvale any more.\nWe need to push back the orcs and secure the forest. We've been able to pick off some of the grunts and scouts by carefully sneaking around the edges of their camp.\nFight the orcs and bring me the jagged swords and curved knives that they use. I'll make sure their weapons are salvaged and repurposed, so nothing goes to waste.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":49.4,"y":67,"n":"Shandrina","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"2757":{"id":2757,"t":"Booty Bay or Bust!","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with McGavan in Booty Bay.\nMithril Insignia\nProvided: Mithril Insignia","desc":"Listen, kid, you're not gonna learn anything hanging around here.\nI know a guy who knows a guy. He hangs around the smithy in Booty Bay. If you show him this insignia, he'll tell you all about mithril.\nSo whadd'ya say? Leave this kid stuff to the babies in diapers, ‹name› -- it's time to move on.\nIf you're interested, his name's McGavan. Show him this trinket and he'll recognize your commitment.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","back":"A rare breed your kind be, matey. Let me see that insignia.","done":"By Blackhoof's back hair -- finally, one worthy of the Mithril Order!\nOrgrimmar Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.4,"y":23.5,"n":"Ox","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.9,"y":75.4,"n":"McGavan","e":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97957":{"id":97957,"t":"Camping 101 herbalism","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Faruza in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your herbalism skill to 20","desc":"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.8,"y":52,"n":"Faruza","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94357":{"id":94357,"t":"Craftsmans writ cenarion herb bag","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Cenarion Herb Bag\nCenarion Herb Bag","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Cenarion Herb Bag, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Cenarion Herb Bag Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94357","cats":["crafting"]},"94277":{"id":94277,"t":"Craftsmans writ truesilver rod","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Truesilver Rod\nTruesilver Rod","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Truesilver Rod, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Truesilver Rod Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94277","cats":["crafting"]},"7877":{"id":7877,"t":"The Treasure of the Shen'dralar","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 675, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Return to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar. Claim your reward!","desc":"In the library, Athenaeum, you will find an ancient chest hidden beneath the stairway. Take from it that which you desire.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBonecrusher Backwood Helm Sedge Boots\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","done":"You open the chest to find...\nStart Shen'dralar Ancient End Treasure of the Shen'dralar Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Horde Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 7877\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 10,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Madness Within\nYou must destroy the guardians surrounding the 5 Pylons that power the Prison of Immol'thar.\nShen'dralar Ancient\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Treasure of the Shen'dralar this quest\nReturn to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar.\nShen'dralar Ancient\n650 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"837":{"id":837,"t":"Encroachment","lv":10,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 4 Razormane Quilboars, 4 Razormane Scouts, 4 Razormane Dustrunners and 4 Razormane Battleguards for Gar'Thok at Razor Hill.\nRazormane Quilboar slain : 0/ 4\nRazormane Scout slain : 0/ 4\nRazormane Dustrunner slain : 0/ 4\nRazormane Battleguard slain : 0/ 4","desc":"When we arrived, the Razormane quilboars possessed much of the land, and proved a thorn in our sides. Through our efforts we have driven out the largest part of their numbers, but still they remain well-fortified in some areas.\nIt has gone on long enough, however. For our own protection, we cannot allow the Razormane any hold in our lands. Their camps can be found to the west of here. Look for the brambles and you will find them. Today we drive them from Durotar, tomorrow, perhaps from all of Kalimdor.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+75 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Though they do possess some intelligence and some organization, I find it constantly amazing that the quilboars were able to capture and hold so much territory in Kalimdor. Perhaps they are more crafty an enemy than I give them credit for...","done":"I will pass along word that the quilboars have been removed from their lairs, and that their structures may be set to fire. The removal of the Razormane from Durotar brings us closer to fully securing the borders of our new homeland.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.9,"y":43.5,"n":"Gar'Thok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"37":{"id":37,"t":"Find the Lost Guards","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Guard Thomas wants you to travel north up the river and search for the two lost guards, Rolf and Malakai.","desc":"A few days ago we sent two Guards, Rolf and Malakai, to investigate along the river, and they have not yet returned. To complete my report, I must know what happened to those men.\nTravel north along the river and find the guards... or their remains.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Although much has been stripped from the corpse, strewn nearby is a medallion with the words: \"Footman Malakai Stone\" etched upon it.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":74,"y":72.2,"n":"Guard Thomas","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":72.7,"y":60.3,"n":"A half-eaten body","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3637":{"id":3637,"t":"Gnome Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Gnome Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Engineering at the expert level breaks into two disciplines: gnome and goblin. While I think it is a waste, you should be aware of gnome specialization. They make items and gadgets that claim to change the world, but rarely work.\n‹name›, read this manual. If you wish to learn how to make metal paper weights, then take the manual to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure you are sure before finishing his task.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"Hello there! If you've come about a homing robot that may have smashed through a wall of your domicile, then I will refer you to my barrister in advance. Otherwise, what can I do for you today?","done":"You've come to learn about gnome engineering, eh? Well, you've come to the right gnome. While the ruling faction of Gnomeregan may use politics to ostracize those they view as an intellectual threat, they know that knowledge is something they cannot control.\nThey and I both know that when I left Gnomeregan, they lost one of their greatest gnome engineers alive today. If you're a capable student, I'll teach you what I know.\nThe Barrens Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tinkerwiz","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"5157":{"id":5157,"t":"Collection of the Corrupt Water","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Empty Canteen to the Moon Well in the center of Jaedenar and fill it before returning to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\nCorrupt Moonwell Water\nProvided: Empty Canteen","desc":"Deep within Jaedenar lies Shadow Hold--the main fortress of their corruption and evil.\nThe Shadow Council has protective spells surrounding their lair in the form of braziers. If I am to find out any more information about our enemy through scrying, then those braziers must be extinguished. By doing so, I should be able to spy on the Council and find out who leads them.\nIf you can, take this canteen and fill it at the Moon Well in the center of Jaedenar. Return to me afterwards.","rew":"Experience: 3,800","back":"Once we have the waters from the Moon Well, we will purify it and use it to extinguish the braziers of protection within Shadow Hold. That should allow me ample time to see into the chambers even deeper and discern who actually leads this... cult.\nI pray the Earthmother is with us.","done":"This will do nicely, ‹name›.\nNow all we have to do besides apply the waters to the braziers is to have it purified. That should not be difficult--it should only require a little travel.\nHopefully we can do this quickly.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.2,"y":82.1,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4117":{"id":4117,"t":"Corrupted Whipper Root","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a whipper root plant. The visible roots of the plant appear tough and leathery, and a slimy film hangs from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 3 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Whipper Root. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":40.1,"y":85.2,"n":"Corrupted Whipper Root","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"517":{"id":517,"t":"Elixir of Agony","lv":30,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a keg of Shindigger Stout to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\nKeg of Shindigger Stout Keg of Shindigger Stout","desc":"This new elixir is finally ready to be tested. But why let a perfectly good, highly contagious plague go to waste on a mere frog or dog? Let's have us some true fun in the name of Lady Sylvanas.\nHead down to Dun Garok. You know the barracks where those filthy little dwarves skitter about. Steal me a keg of their Shindigger Stout. Once I have that keg, you and I will have quite the party, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Sometimes I get so bored out here in Tarren Mill I like to open up the formaldehyde jar and let the lovely aroma waft through the air. Makes Umpi a little nervous though.\nSo were you able to get a keg from the Dwarves? I swear if I have to stare at this deadly elixir without using on it someone for another day I am going to scream.","done":"Finally! Now we are ready for action!","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"9317":{"id":9317,"t":"Consecrated Sharpening Stones","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 58.","obj":"8 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nConsecrated Sharpening Stone","back":"If you bring me eight necrotic runes from the Scourge invaders, I can give you a consecrated sharpening stone. It should be of great help in your battle against the minions of the Lich King.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Here are your consecrated sharpening stones. Use them prudently.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.8,"y":30.7,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":72.6,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.1,"y":45.4,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8997":{"id":8997,"t":"Back to the Beginning","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Deliana at The High Seat in Ironforge.","desc":"I suppose that this is goodbye then, my friend. But, I'll always be here if you want to come back and talk with me from time to time. Probably while you're loitering around waiting for your buddies to join you for a raid on Blackrock Spire.\nGo, before I start to cry. Go back to Deliana in Ironforge and tell her what's happened.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"I am very happy to see you return to me safely, ‹name›. You look well, if not a bit worse for the wear.\nCome, tell me of all that has transpired.\nBurning Steppes Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8677":{"id":8677,"t":"Darkhorn the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.1,"y":33.8,"n":"Elder Darkhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"93797":{"id":93797,"t":"Boughs in the wind","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring a Wind-Infused Bough to Belann Windwood in Valanaar.\nWind-Infused Bough","desc":"It is a time-honored tradition for young mages to create their own spell focus when they have shown a certain degree of magical proficiency. This is typically done by gathering a fallen branch from our oldest trees, as they have some lingering traces of elemental wind.\nI have found the most ideal ones to be near the wind shrine, just south of Falaath Village. Go and bring me back a large branch and I will teach you about the traditions as we create your spell focus.","rew":"You will receive:\nWindbough Wand 5 Elixir of Minor Spirit\nExperience: 850\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"Every year that passes in Zephras sees fewer and fewer of those who are gifted with a talent for magic.\nI am glad to see young mages such as yourself participate in our oldest traditions to help keep our history and culture alive and well.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I can indeed feel the elemental energies in this bough waiting to be harnessed by those that have the gift to do so. This will make an excellent spell focus.\nDid this branch sing to you, perhaps? It has often been the case that the branch picks the ‹class›, and not the other way around.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":62.8,"y":77.4,"n":"Belann Windwood","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1957":{"id":1957,"t":"Mana Surges","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Mana Surges in the allowed time limit.\nMana Surge slain : 0/ 12","desc":"We are almost finished, but this last step is the most perilous, ‹name›.\nI have the empty summoner's orb and am ready to empower it. We will do this by harnessing the energy of a mana rift. I'll cast a spell that will temporarily open a rift, from which creatures, mana surges, will pour out. You must defeat the mana surges and their power will be released, which I will then collect.\nKill enough mana surges before the rift closes and I will place all their collected energy in your orb.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"You have not killed the required amount of mana surges, ‹name›.","done":"You did it! I never doubted you for a second! Ok, maybe for just a second, or two... but basically I didn't have much doubt.\nHonest.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"757":{"id":757,"t":"Rite of Strength","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Bristlebacks in Brambleblade Ravine and bring 12 Bristleback Belts to Chief Hawkwind in Camp Narache.\n12 Bristleback Belt Bristleback Shaman 80 % , Bristleback Quilboar 80 %","desc":"The Rites of the Earthmother are the steps a young tauren needs to take to gain respect in Thunder Bluff.\nFirst you must pass the Rite of Strength. In this test you must prove your bravery by slaying enemies of the tribe.\nBristlebacks of Brambleblade Ravine to the east are encroaching on our tribal lands. They ambush our hunting parties and steal from the village by dark.\nShow your valor by slaying these villains and return to the Chief in Camp Narache with their belts as proof of your deeds.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRock Mace Stone Tomahawk Whittling Knife Elder's Cane Brave's Axe\nExperience: 450\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you completed the Rite of Strength, ‹name›? I require proof of your valor against the enemy of our tribe, the Bristlebacks.","done":"You have passed the first test of the Rites of the Earthmother. The tribe will be proud.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":42.5,"y":90.1,"n":"Seer Graytongue","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":43.9,"y":76.7,"n":"Chief Hawkwind","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9077":{"id":9077,"t":"Bonescythe Breastplate","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Bonescythe Breastplate if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Breastplate, 25 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 2 Arcanite Bars and 6 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Breastplate\n25 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcanite Bar\n6 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Breastplate\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n,you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Bonescythe Breastplate.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9237":{"id":9237,"t":"Glacial Cloak","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 2 Essences of Water, 4 Ironweb Spider Silks and 200 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.\n5 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n4 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\n2 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n4 Ironweb Spider Silk Mother Smolderweb 50 % , Crystal Fang 47 % , Gretheer 16.2 % , Plague Lurker 13.9 % and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create a Glacial cloak. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nGlacial Cloak","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8917":{"id":8917,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Shadowcraft Bracers to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nShadowcraft Bracers Scholomance Occultist 6.3 % in Scholomance , Instructor Malicia 5 % in Scholomance , Dark Shade 3.8 % , Risen Construct 3.5 % in Scholomance and 2 more","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Mux will be quite happy with this.\nThose bracers were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance, I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"91317":{"id":91317,"t":"The tarnished","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 8 Tarnished Drudges, 6 Tarnished Zealots, and collect the head of Commander Rudolph Gelhardt in Tirisfal Glades.\nRudolph Gelhardt's Head\nTarnished Drudge slain : 0/ 8\nTarnished Zealot slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Not all risen paladins have acclimated well to our new existence, as you may have seen yourself already. Some have carried forward their prejudices from life, and continue to visit violence upon their fellow Forsaken.\nAs it stands we are mistrusted by our people who remember well the persecution inflicted by the living in the name of the light, and these attacks do not help. A number of these tarnished have taken up residence at Shadowvale to the southwest. End them and bring me their leader's head.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"The Tarnished threaten what little goodwill we have with the other Forsaken. As much as it pains me to cross blades with our former brothers and sisters, they must be stopped if our fledgling order is to survive.","done":"Excellent work, Cola. Every time one of these Tarnished strike out and kill one of the Forsaken, it becomes that much easier for our detractors to stoke mistrust towards us paladins. Eliminating them will help further our cause and solidify our place here in Tirisfal.\nI suspect it may take a long time for us to be fully embraced by the Forsaken and the horde. It could take years... or maybe even decades, but the best we can do is keep trying to prove ourselves.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"2997":{"id":2997,"t":"Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.","desc":"Hello, ‹name›. I know you're busy helping out the people of Dun Morogh, but when you have the time, you should make your way up to Ironforge to speak to one of our most respected ilk: Tiza Battleforge. She's the one the younger paladins go to when it's time they learn more about the Light and what's expected of ya.\nYou can find her upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries. If you've never been there, it's in the Mystic Ward. Good luck to ya, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Well met, ‹name›. I hope the Light shows you the true path and keeps you safe from evil.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.6,"y":52.1,"n":"Azar Stronghammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7637":{"id":7637,"t":"Emphasis on Sacrifice","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -150g instead of 0.","obj":"Travel to Ironforge and get High Priest Rohan's Exorcism Censer. You will need to make a donation of 150 gold in order to secure it.","desc":"In order to prepare yourself for this task, you must first show due sacrifice and judgment... with an emphasis on sacrifice.\nYou must acquire High Priest Rohan's exorcism censer for your task. Even though its use will be for good and just reasons, due compensation must be given for it.\nProceed to Ironforge and speak with the High Priest. By bringing ample coin with you to help offset the loss of his censer, it will show your due sacrifice.\nGo now ‹name›, time is of the essence.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Greetings, noble ‹class›! I have prepared my trusted censer with the freshest of incense and blessed it thrice for your use. Your donation will help us in Ironforge not only create a new censer, but also to bolster sagging reserves of food for our needy.","done":"Blessings onto you, friend ‹class›! Your donation goes far beyond what was needed. Your sacrifice will not only help us recover what we have lost, but also help us to help those most in need here in Ironforge.\nNow, let me make sure I've suitably prepared this censer for your future needs...\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5637":{"id":5637,"t":"Desperate Prayer","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.","desc":"Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, ‹name›. High Priest Rohan in the Hall of Mysteries wants to speak to you. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priest to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that he wants to speak to ya.\nBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.","rew":"You will learn: Desperate Prayer\nExperience: 210","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, ‹name›. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"Priestess Josetta","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8837":{"id":8837,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Darnassus. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Lunalight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"79637":{"id":79637,"t":"A ticking present","lv":40,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 213443","done":"Have a joyous Feast of Great-Winter from your friends at Smokeywood Pastures.\nLevel 40 , requires level 20 Difficulty 20 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 79637","cats":["seasonal"]},"8357":{"id":8357,"t":"Dancing for Marzipan","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a dance emote at Innkeeper Saelienne, and in exchange you'll receive Darnassus Marzipan!","desc":"Even though you're trick-or-treating for a sick child, you still need to perform a trick for the treat! We can't very well change the tradition, now can we...\nI believe the cost of a piece of marzipan nowadays is to bust out and DANCE! That's right, let me see your moves! Dance for me, and I'll give you some tasty marzipan!","rew":"You will receive:\nDarnassus Marzipan","back":"You know how to dance, don't you? Try by putting your right foot in... then your right foot out... your right foot in... shake it all about...","done":"You're quite the dancing machine, ‹name›!\nHere's your treat for being such a good sport. Happy Hallow's End, and give my best to your sick little friend! I hope they get better soon.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":67.4,"y":15.6,"n":"Innkeeper Saelienne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"98517":{"id":98517,"t":"Call of fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to Sessaria Skystride or Aarnor Galestrike on Zephras Isle to continue your training as a Shaman.\nYou can return to Zephras via the skycutter transport that docks in Mulgore at Skywatcher Plateau, northwest of Thunder Bluff.\nTorch of the Dormant Flame","desc":"Greetings, young Skyborne. The spirits have spoken of you, and tell me that you are ready to heed the call of fire. However, I shall not be the one to start you on that Path. Return to your home in the elemental plane, seek your mentors there. They will tell you what must be done.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Horde Quest ID 98517","cats":["shaman"]},"8277":{"id":8277,"t":"Deadly Desert Venom","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Beetix Ficklespragg at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to gather 8 Stonelash Scorpid Stingers and 8 Sand Skitterer Fangs. Return to her when you have completed the task.\n8 Stonelash Scorpid Stinger Stonelash Scorpid 80 %\n8 Sand Skitterer Fang Sand Skitterer 80 %","desc":"Beetix Ficklespragg at your service! My cousin Noggle makes a living gathering rare herbs for Cenarion Hold alchemists. Or used to, anyway. He came back from his last trip with a strong poison running though his veins.\nI've managed to slow down the venom, but to fully neutralize it I need poison samples from whatever stung him.\nNoggle arrived from the north, so I'd bet my shirt stonelash scorpids or sand skitterers did it. Bring me some stingers and fangs and I'll try to make an antidote for him.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Are you done collecting those samples? We could lose Noggle any minute now!","done":"Cross your fingers, friend! Here's to hoping we can save Noggle!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.6,"y":38.6,"n":"Beetix Ficklespragg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"437":{"id":437,"t":"The Dead Fields","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill rot hide gnolls at the Dead Fields.\nWhen Nightlash appears, kill her.\nBring the Essence of Nightlash to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.\nEssence of Nightlash Nightlash","desc":"Our initial scouting reports of Silverpine show the rot hides have a base at an old farm to the north, the Dead Fields. We have sent small assaults against them, but each time they are reinforced by the banshee Nightlash, who uses her magic to rout our forces.\nWe want Nightlash destroyed.\nGo to the Dead Fields and assault the rot hides. If you don't see Nightlash then kill the rot hides until she appears, then defeat her.\nHer essence will turn to dust. Bring me that dust as proof.","rew":"You will receive:\nReconnaissance Boots\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you defeated Nightlash, ‹name›? Our success against the rot hides depends on her destruction!","done":"I heard of your successful raid against the rot hides, ‹name›, and this essence is proof of Nightlash's death.\nThe Scourge have lost ground this day. Your value to the Forsaken grows.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1077":{"id":1077,"t":"Special Delivery for Gaxim","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 825 experience instead of 850, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Scroll of Messaging to Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon.\nScroll of Messaging\nProvided: Scroll of Messaging","desc":"Here you are, ‹name›. This should do nicely.\nPlease give my regards to Gaxim when next you see him. I look forward to hearing about this adventure when it sees its completion.\nFare well.","rew":"Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Haha! you're back! Do you have it? Do you have the spell?","done":"This is perfect, ‹name›! Well done.\nThis spell, mixed with the NG-5, shall make the perfect remote explosive.\nWe'll be able to create the perfect distraction for you so you can sneak in and steal the Venture Co.'s letters and engineering plans.\nThat will surely slow down their deforestation acts.\nStormwind City Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53,"y":86.6,"n":"Collin Mauren","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"97237":{"id":97237,"t":"Shelf picked","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find each of the reading materials located somewhere in the library and then return to Roy Lewells in Stormwind's Park.\nField Accounts of Horde Razings\nTrollbane Conquests\nThe Forsaken Ally\nCycles of Morality","desc":"I've checked our inventory and all of the selections Mr. Lewells has listed are currently available.\nYou will, however, need to procure them off the shelves yourself. Part of our librarian duty is vigilance, and for that, I will resume supervisory bookkeeping.\nReturning with the material to Roy on his behalf will not mark yourself accountable for their return; as with his note you're serving as the book club's official courier. Their establishment shall carry that burden.\nGood day, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRumsey Rum Light 5 Ice Cold Milk\nMoney: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,000","back":"You forgot what you had to do the moment you stepped through the door, eh? Happens to everyone.","done":"These are them! Some of them even smell exotic! Fantastic, I can't wait for us to have lively conversations about these writings.\nCellar after hours, of course.\nThanks for the quick errand run, Gad. As promised, it's on the house. We keep our word here.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":71.6,"y":7.4,"n":"Donyal Tovald","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":62,"n":"Roy Lewells","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"1477":{"id":1477,"t":"Vital Supplies","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Watchmaster Sorigal.","desc":"Our mages are conducting research at Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands, research vital to our understanding of the Dark Portals. They require nearly constant supplies, but our supply line to Nethergarde is tenuous.\nYou must help ensure the supplies make it to Nethergard. Report to Watchmaster Sorigal in Darkshire, and do as he asks. This task will take you into hostile lands, ‹name›. Prepare yourself.","rew":"Experience: 975\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Andromath sent you? Very good. I have an important task for you...\nStormwind City Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.7,"y":87.6,"n":"High Sorcerer Andromath","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":46.2,"n":"Watchmaster Sorigal","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"597":{"id":597,"t":"The Bloodsail Buccaneers","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report your findings to First Mate Crazz in Booty Bay.","desc":"The map shows Booty Bay with a red \"X\" drawn precisely at the spot at which you are standing.\nThe scribbled text reads:\n\"You men are to secure a camp at this location and keep quiet. Wait for the signal from the southern command post before attacking. If anyone approaches you, kill them.\"","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+75 reputation with Booty Bay\n-375 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"Sure, I remember you, ‹class›. Back from scouting I see....","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":69.5,"n":"Bloodsail Correspondence","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.1,"y":76.2,"n":"First Mate Crazz","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"197":{"id":197,"t":"Raptor Mastery","lv":43,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill Tethis, an elusive, dangerous raptor in Stranglethorn.\nTalon of Tethis Tethis","desc":"Because you proved yourself to be such a go-getter in the jungle, let me tell you about a ferocious raptor that even I have failed to kill. Ajeck here calls this wily raptor Tethis.\nIf you want to prove yourself a true master, kill Tethis and bring me his talon. It would be a feat that no other big game hunter has accomplished.","rew":"You will receive:\nRaptor Hunter Tunic\nExperience: 3,600","back":"How goes the hunt for Tethis? Tracked her all the way back to camp, did you?","done":"Master ‹name›, the raptor slayer!\nHas a nice ring to it, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8597":{"id":8597,"t":"Draconic for Dummies","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Narain Soothfancy's book, buried on an island in the South Seas.","desc":"I knew that book would come in handy some day! Thankfully, I had the wit and foresight to stow it somewhere safe.\nDon't worry, it's in a place that nobody could ever hope to find it! I needed a gyrocopter just to get there the first time. Unfortunately I crashed it on the beach on my way back. It was through that accident that I gained these super-gnomish psychic powers!\nLook for my crashed gyrocopter somewhere on Land's End Beach and swim south from there! You'll know the spot when you see it!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"The book is gone! On top of the dirt mound is a note.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.8,"y":129.7,"n":"Freshly Dug Dirt","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8757":{"id":8757,"t":"The Path of the Invoker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.\nThe signet ring of the invoker will greatly enhance your magical and natural abilities.\nBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"997":{"id":997,"t":"Denalan's Earth","lv":5,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the package of Rare Earth to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.\nRare Earth\nProvided: Rare Earth","desc":"Are you heading to the south? To Lake Al'Ameth? If so, then I have a task I might ask of you...\nMy colleague Denalan has a camp along the eastern end of the lake, where he is studying and experimenting on the plant life of Teldrassil. He requested a package of rare earths from Darnassus and it was late, only recently arriving here in Dolanaar.\nCan you take the package to him?","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 230\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You have something for me?","done":"Ah, it's here! I have waited for this rare earth for quite some time. I hope it's still fresh...\nThank you for bringing it to me, ‹name›. You are a ‹race› who is generous with his time.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":57.7,"n":"Syral Bladeleaf","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"917":{"id":917,"t":"Webwood Egg","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Webwood Egg to Gilshalan in Aldrassil.\nWebwood Egg Webwood Eggs","desc":"Now that I have the spiders' venom, I'd like some live specimens to study. Unfortunately, capturing a living, giant spider is more than I can ask of you, young ‹class›. And a giant spider is more than I could handle myself!\nBut if you can find an unhatched egg, then delivering specimens will be much easier, and I can then arrange for the unhatched spiders to be contained.\nThere must be a nest deep in the Shadowthread Cave. Please, search for an egg in the nest and return it to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWoodland Shield Woodland Tunic Woodland Robes\nExperience: 550\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you been inside the Shadowthread Cave, ‹name›? Did you find a spider egg?","done":"Ah, very good. I will have this egg and the venom transported to Darnassus, then return there when my studies are done here. I expect to find out a great deal from these specimens, ‹name›. You have been a great help to me.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.8,"y":41.7,"n":"Gilshalan Windwalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"357":{"id":357,"t":"The Lich's Identity","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Lich's Spellbook to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.\nThe Lich's Spellbook Gunther's Books","desc":"There is a lich who dwells on the island in Brightwater Lake to the north. Although he is a free-willed Forsaken, he believes all other Undead are Scourge slaves and has his minions attack anyone who approaches him.\nBut because he is Forsaken, the Queen will want him. And if he is skilled in Necromancy, then his knowledge would be...quite useful to us.\nTo discover his identity and his talents, I must see his spellbook. Steal into his camp and acquire it, then return to me.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 525\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"‹name›, have you acquired the book?","done":"Very good, ‹name›. I will study this book and determine the identity of that lich. You have served your Queen well.\n<Bethor opens the book and stares intently at its glowing pages...>\nAstonishing! The book you retrieved belongs to no one other than Gunther Arcanus!\nGunther was a skilled Necromancer in life; he and I were friends and comrades-in-arms, before the Plague. And judging from his book he has grown even more powerful in death.\nHis skills would be a great boon to us.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":84.1,"y":17.4,"n":"Bethor Iceshard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1717":{"id":1717,"t":"Gakin's Summons","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.","desc":"‹name›! Didn't expect to see you around these parts, but I was instructed to keep an eye out for you.\nIt's past time you got some more training, so you should stop in to see Gakin the next time you're in Stormwind. He'll be waiting for you.","rew":"Experience: 390","done":"I'm glad someone was able to get a hold of you, ‹name›. I was beginning to fear the worst. It would be a shame to lose you, after the time we've invested in you. We can talk later, though. Your training is the only important thing now.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.7,"y":22.6,"n":"Lago Blackwrench","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5237":{"id":5237,"t":"Mission Accomplished!","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nValiant Shortsword Intrepid Shortsword\nYou will also receive:\nHeroic Commendation Medal\nExperience: 9,300\n+200 reputation with Alliance\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"‹name›, your successful re-engineering of the cauldrons is a tremendous victory for us!\n<The high executor clears his throat and begins to bellow loudly.>\nLet all within my presence hear: for service to the Forsaken and to the Horde as a whole above and beyond what was expected - in the face of overwhelming odds and incredible danger, might I add - I give ‹name› this, and I extend upon his/her our undying gratitude as a true hero of the Horde. Huzzah!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"117":{"id":117,"t":"Thunderbrew Lager","lv":15,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Thunderbrew Lager.","obj":"Bring Grimbooze Thunderbrew 5 hops to complete his special brew.\n5 Hops Harvest Reaper 37.1 % , Foe Reaper 4000 36 % , Harvest Watcher 33.4 % , Harvest Golem 29.7 % and 1 more","desc":"Hurry, my friend, move with haste\nIn order for our rich lager to taste\nMore like beer and less like stew,\nHops are needed to make the brew.","rew":"You will receive:\nKeg of Thunderbrew","back":"Hurry, my friend, move with haste\nIn order for our rich lager to taste\nMore like beer and less like stew,\nHops are needed to make the brew.","done":"Hops and Barley, yeast and malt\nThe taste-buds feel a virtual assault,\nNo need to plead, no need to beg\nFor Thunderbrew Lager comes in a keg!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":44.6,"y":80.3,"n":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"98197":{"id":98197,"t":"Spoils of war","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover 6 Khaz Modan Timber and 30 Khaz Modan Iron from Menethil Harbor for Valstag Ironjaw.\n6 Khaz Modan Timber\n30 Khaz Modan Iron","desc":"This harbor was first built by the Old Horde as a staging ground for their naval invasion of Hillsbrad. Completely circumvented Lordaeron's defenses!\nSo many lives lost...\nWhat's worse is that fleet was built with the very resources they stole from Khaz Modan!\nPlenty of it remains in the harbor after Admiral Proudmoore routed the brutes and built this place for the Alliance. We'll need it to bolster the town's defenses with the Dragonmaw on the move.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Keep your wits about you beneath the waves. There's plenty of nasties down there!","done":"Ah! A bit damp, but nothing a few days in the sun won't fix.\nThank you, ‹class›. It's nice to not solely rely on shipments from Theramore or Auberdine for once!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10,"y":56.8,"n":"Valstag Ironjaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"277":{"id":277,"t":"Fire Taboo","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Rethiel the Greenwarden 9 Crude Flints.\n9 Crude Flint Mosshide Alpha 80 % , Mosshide Mystic 80 % , Mosshide Brute 80 % , Mosshide Trapper 80 % and 3 more","desc":"The Mosshides are cutting the trees of the Wetlands, using the trees' flesh to warm themselves with fire. I will suffer this pain no longer!\nRid the Mosshides of their crude flints, the tools they use to make fire. The flints are borne by all Mosshides except the smaller Mosshide gnolls and Mosshide mongrels.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Spongy Morel\nExperience: 1,850","back":"Do you have the Gnolls' tools for fire?","done":"... thank you. I will smash these flints and cast them into the sea, so that they may never again be used to burn living wood.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":56.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Rethiel the Greenwarden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"88757":{"id":88757,"t":"Accessories of the lost","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring back Essene's Necklace, Essene's Spellbook, and Essene's Waterskin.\nEssene's Necklace\nEssene's Spellbook\nEssene's Waterskin","desc":"While I was fleeing from those Dark Irons, I wound up dropping lots of my gear!\nIt looks like I lost... my green leather waterskin, my spellbook, my necklace, and... well I need these things!\nIf you can find them while I repack and catch my breath, that would be a great help.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":51.4,"y":9,"n":"Essene Villard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92597":{"id":92597,"t":"Reading the ley lines","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use your Read Ley Line racial ability at the ley line in Thendal Grove.\nUse your Read Ley Line ability near the Thendal Grove Ley Line","desc":"Here in the elemental plane, we derive much of our arcane strength from ley lines that still run through the ground under our feet. Of late, these ley lines have begun to pierce the surface, giving us more direct and powerful access to these latent arcane energies.\nGo to the standing stones to the northeast. There is a ley line there. Tap into your birthright and draw in its energy.","done":"Do you feel it? Yes? Good! You have taken your first steps. You'll find that with your abilities, you will be able to tap into latent magical energy in many locations. Doing so will provide a myriad of benefits, some profound, others more subtle. You won't know until you tap into them, But that's the best part of the gift... making the unknown known.\nIf we are to survive these dire times, we must be unwavering in our search for knowledge... and power.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.2,"y":24.8,"n":"Falorne Fallwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92517":{"id":92517,"t":"The criminal element","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 10 Highlands Bandits and their leader, \"Badwind\" Bennic in the Shen'dar Highlands.\nHighlands Bandit slain : 0/ 10\n\"Badwind\" Bennic slain","desc":"There's a cave not far to the north, hidden behind a waterfall. It's well known to me that there's a group of bandits that are operating out of that cave. They were a problem for us before the cult arrived, but now they are a real terror. I can't spare the people to go and clear them out, unfortunately.\nI need you to go there and take care of them for me. Kill as many as you can, and if possible, take out their leader, the one they call \"Badwind\" Bennic. That cave is dangerous, so be careful.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBandit's Jerkin Patchwork Leggings Highlands Mail Legguards\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 480\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"With the bandits dispersed, that is one less problem for us to deal with. Though I confess that now I worry that any bandits who survived may turn next to the cult for protection, further bolstering their increasingly alarming numbers.\nStill though, we'll take the victories where we can get them.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93317":{"id":93317,"t":"Crab season","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 pieces of Windsong Crawler Meat.\n6 Windsong Crawler Meat","desc":"Are you familiar with Windsong Crawlers? You see, these crabs are native only to Windsong Lake here on Zephras, and they are only able to be harvested a few weeks of the year.\nWith all of the cult activity of late, I've not been able to get out to the lake to harvest them, and our window is rapidly closing. I'd be appreciative if you could go and gather some for me. They can generally be found along the shorelines around the lake and in rivers.\nDo be careful though, they are meaner than they look!","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Pincer Bites 5 Pincer Bites\nMoney: 2 0 gold, 2 silver, 0 copper Experience: 600","back":"Windsong Crawler meat is common enough here but it was something of a delicacy on the islands of Anvilas and Siroccas. Was a time, back when the skystreams were open that the locals would mob me for the stuff when I'd make the trip to Shen'dramar or New Eldre'naar.\nNot been able to visit those places in... well... a long time.","done":"Winds bless me this meat looks fantastic!\nThank you so much, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":60.6,"y":72.6,"n":"Nyalah Brightfire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8117":{"id":8117,"t":"Vision of Voodress","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Vision of Voodress","rew":"You will receive:\nVision of Voodress\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Good news, ‹name›. Molthor be singin' your praises lately. He say how you be turnin' into a real hero of Zandalar.\nHe also say for Maywiki to polish your orb some more! Give it here so Maywiki can brighten the vision.","done":"Beware the evil Hakkari spirits, mon. Honestly, they be spooky.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});